IPOD(tm) DOCK - DIGITAL AUDIO
-------------------------

VERSION: 0.91

DESCRIPTION:

The XMOS iPod Dock Reference Design allows bit-perfect digital audio streaming from iPod or iPhone(tm) devices over USB, yielding superior audio quality.
The complete source code, together with the free XDE and XMOS reconfigurable devices allow the implementer to select the exact mix of interfaces and processing required. 
DSP algorithms can be implemented using the available bandwidth of the XCore processors.

REQUIRED TOOLS:

XMOS Desktop Development Tools 9.9.0 or above

REQUIRED HARDWARE:

XMOS Digital iPod dock 1v1 or above

APPLICATION NOTE:

Please see the following documents for more information:

iPod Dock Reference Design Application Note
iPod Dock Reference Design Hardware Manual

INSTALLATION AND RUNNING THE DEMO (COMMAND LINE):

From an enviroment that can access the XMOS Desktop Development tools.
Unzip the zipfile and from the top level directory run:

       xmake all

INSTALLATION AND RUNNING THE DEMO (XDE):

To install, open the XDE Eclipse IDE and perform the following steps:

   * Select the "Import" item from the "File" menu
   * Select "General" -> "Existing Projects into Workspace" and click "Next"
   * Click on "Browse" next to "Select archive file" and select the
     button server zipfile 
   * Make sure the project you want to import is ticks in the
     "Projects:" list
   * Click on "Finish"

To build, select the project in the Project Explorer window and click
on build icon.

To run, click on the run icon. To configure the project to run on a
particular device or in the simulator click on the drop down arrow
next to the run icon and select "Run Configurations"
